00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.010
I literally, I was like,
what is this thing?

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:13.843
And you've got mail.

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:14.950
I remember when it came out and I saw it

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.989
and I was obsessed with typewriters.

00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:17.822
- [Greg] Oh yeah.

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:20.210
- [Kelly] Yes. That's when my obsession--

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.750
- You were like a lone reed.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.680
One of the great Nora
Ephron lines of all time.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.160
Me wooing Meg Ryan.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.370
- [Kelly] What a great character.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.450
- Well I'm a fan of yours.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.110
Honestly, I feel like Kelly Clarkson

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.893
is my fourth daughter.

00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:35.726
- [Kelly] What?

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:36.559
- Yes.

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:37.450
- I'm not even, I'm too old

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.283
to be a daughter of yours.

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:40.490
- I about like 20

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.620
whatever, however long ago that was,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.250
you had your meteoric rise.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.140
- Oh, 20 years ago.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.520
- Was it? It was 20 years ago.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.380
We were at maximum stress point.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.530
We had a lot of kids.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.760
I guess it technically is only

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.330
three daughters, but it felt like 30.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.163
- That's a lot.

00:00:57.163 --> 00:01:00.650
- Yes. And they were like
ages, you know, young.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.980
Just the time where they
are sticking fingers

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.170
in light plugs and everything.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.090
And when you could get them to bed,

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.420
and when you could
finally find some solace

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.520
and you know, I'd sit down with my wife.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.483
I'd have a little cocktail.

00:01:14.575 --> 00:01:16.430
Little cocktail.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.397
And we would watch that show
and just watch you crush it.

00:01:19.397 --> 00:01:21.167
And I believe we voted for you.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.113
- Well, I'm gonna take
it like that anyway.

00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:24.177
(crowd cheering)

00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:25.684
That's so nice.

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:27.530
- It's crazy that it's 20 years ago,

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.006
but you're musical as well.

00:01:29.006 --> 00:01:30.310
Cause I've seen you sing in movies.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.500
- Oh stop.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.670
- I've seen it.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:33.860
So stop.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.990
No do you love, did you ever think about

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.020
going into music or have a band

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.210
or anything when you were like younger?

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.090
- You feel threatened?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.000
- I feel threatened.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.840
No, I feel challenged that maybe

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.050
there's a duet in our future.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.570
- Oh my gosh, is that happening?

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.927
Are we finally doing this thing?

00:01:45.927 --> 00:01:48.000
- This is finally gonna happen.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.573
It could be from Greg to Kelly.

00:01:49.573 --> 00:01:53.340
- I did a movie with Matt Damon about

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.570
these conjoined twins back
when everyone in Hollywood

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.870
was making movies about conjoined twins.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.730
And it was this comedy, the
Farrelly brothers did it.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:06.970
And at the end of the movie,
we get separated and my dream,

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.750
Matt's an introvert and I'm an extrovert.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.500
And I have this dream of
doing musical theater.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.780
So Meryl Streep and I perform a number.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.420
And the director says, "Hey,
listen I need you to record,

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.040
I need you to butcher
Billy Stewart's incredible

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.880
1966 version of Summertime."

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.260
So I actually did a full recording of it.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.443
And so eventually,

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.140
I get a call from my lawyer.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.960
This is years later, the movie didn't,

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.280
you know perform very well.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.870
But years later I get a call,
a couple years later of ago

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:42.150
I get a call from my
lawyer who says "Rihanna."

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:42.983
- What?

00:02:42.983 --> 00:02:43.816
- That's right.

00:02:43.816 --> 00:02:48.816
"Rihanna wants to use a part
of your song in her album."

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.330
She wants to kinda, I
guess it's called a--

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.480
- Rihanna sampled you?

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.560
That is amazing.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.800
- She sampled. Yeah.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.037
- [Kelly] I've never been sampled.

00:02:57.037 --> 00:02:58.320
- Yeah. So I'm sampled.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.880
- Yeah. People that are
sampled are awesome.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.354
- I thought we were gonna
like be on the road together.

00:03:03.354 --> 00:03:05.280
(laughs)

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.120
I thought we had a whole thing.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.520
I never talked to her again.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.350
She just used it in this song

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.550
in one of the albums.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.163
So it was cool yeah.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.910
- Greg and Rihanna. Gregory.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.260
It's got a nice combo to it.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.140
- Kind of like a shorter Gregory.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.180
I like it, I like it.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.030
Were your daughters,

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.500
do they freak out that
you're on a Rihanna song?

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.017
- You know, honestly
the song was slightly--

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:31.623
- [Kelly] Inappropriate?

00:03:31.623 --> 00:03:34.883
- Yeah, NR. It was mature audiences only.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.180
So I didn't hear it for years.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.180
And then now I think they're
kinda just discovering it now.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.580
- So wait this got even cooler.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.350
You got sampled on an X-rated song?

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:47.209
This is so much cooler.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:49.000
That's awesome.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.460
So wait I have to ask, in
"Little Miss Sunshine"--

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.000
I love that movie. Everyone does.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.590
Were you really driving the car? The van?

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.383
- Yes. That is not there apparently.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.630
It looks like I'm a little bored there.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.560
(mumbles)

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.410
You can count every Michael
Bay movie ever made,

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.980
this is the most dangerous film ever made.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.920
We didn't have, nobody
was wearing seat belts.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.900
We didn't have clearance on the highway.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.890
We just went out and they handed me--

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.170
Cause I drive in the thing.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.670
They're like, here's the keys.

00:04:21.655 --> 00:04:23.660
- Like they won't even let
me do that in the (mumbles)

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.300
no one can be in the car in like a voicing

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.100
if we're like doing a like
skip forward or something.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.440
Like it's such a liability.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.760
- Yes.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.680
I'm interviewing you during Covid

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.810
on the other side of a couch right now.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.910
(laughs)

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.420
Nobody is making this
movie anymore is my point.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.610
- I love that though.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.610
That would've made me nervous
driving that whole cast.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:44.670
It's a solid cast too.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.190
So you're like, hope I don't mess this up.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.023
- Oh my God.

00:04:47.023 --> 00:04:49.050
There's millions of dollars of cargo

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.760
in this vehicle for God's sake.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.070
- I would not have liked that
pressure is what I'm saying.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.750
So can you tell us what
"Shining Vale" is about?

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.760
The house is beautiful by the way.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:57.633
- It is gorgeous.

00:04:57.633 --> 00:04:58.466
- Yes. It's a gorgeous house.

00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.880
- We shot that out in South Pasadena,

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.830
and then Warner Brothers amazingly

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.770
rebuilt this exact replica

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.860
of this enormous house

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.840
over about three or four sound stages

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.810
at Warner Brothers and
did an incredible job.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.210
But it's this story of

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:16.890
this family,

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.910
I play the father.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:21.120
Courtney Cox, my lovely
wife, America's sweetheart.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.727
There she is ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:22.727 --> 00:05:25.173
(crowd cheering)

00:05:25.173 --> 00:05:26.210
We live in New York City

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.210
and she's had a little
bit of an indiscretion.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.080
And we've had a little bit
of stress in the family.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.530
She used to write kind of these, you know

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.580
those kind of books,
like fifty shades of--

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.775
- Oh naughty books. Naughty books.

00:05:40.775 --> 00:05:42.950
- Yeah naughty books. That lady porn.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.090
- [Kelly] Yes, lady porn.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.350
- And she kinda had a hit
and now she's kind of stuck.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:49.270
So she has writer's block.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.680
We move out to the country
to this little town

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.820
in Connecticut called Shining Vale.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:58.450
And I get this enormous house
for $300,000 below asking.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.370
And we move into it and

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.310
she starts to either

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:07.400
have menopause or starts to see something.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.610
And we're not sure, I'm
not sure what's happening.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:15.053
But there is a spirit,
there is, in the house.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.920
It's some comedy with drama,
it's drama with comedy.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.520
It's a really interesting tone.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.180
The show creators did an incredible job.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.160
It was great fun to do.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.540
And I haven't gotten to
do horror stuff for ever.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.373
So it's great.

00:06:28.373 --> 00:06:29.828
- I love that it ties in both.

00:06:29.828 --> 00:06:31.160
That it's like horror and
there's stuff happening,

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.940
but also there's a lot of comedy.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.030
Like your sarcasm, just
seeping in that scene alone,

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:36.905
was amazing.

00:06:36.905 --> 00:06:37.738
- Oh thanks.

00:06:37.738 --> 00:06:39.220
- And how the daughter,
she's like don't be scared.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.550
She's like, I'm solid.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:41.913
She's like, I love it.

00:06:41.913 --> 00:06:43.730
It's such a teenager.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.700
So ever had any supernatural
experiences like in your life?

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.810
- I have not.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.700
I know everybody has ghost stories.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:51.660
Does everybody have ghost stories?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.377
Anybody have like a serious--

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.400
A smattering of applause.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.800
Not as many ghost people here at the

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.317
Kelly Clarkson show as I would've thought.

00:06:59.317 --> 00:07:00.840
- I think it can be explained.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.750
I think I'm cynical.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.310
I don't believe or not believe.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.630
I just, I think I've had some
stuff happen but I'm like,

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.280
that's probably an old house
or probably like whatever.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.010
- I'm exactly the same.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.500
I don't believe in, you know

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.960
gnomes and elves and fairies.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.070
So ghosts kind of fit in that box.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.150
but I have enough people who have

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.830
told me these stories where I'm like, wow.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.670
That's a pretty convincing story.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.580
I know people that you never would expect

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.210
to have something like
this you know, go down.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.590
So I guess I stay open to it, but no,

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.400
no great ghost story for you.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.850
- I feel like there's
like enough happening

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.850
in this realm to deal with.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.960
That like why invite other realms in?

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.346
- Like we really haven't nailed this one.

00:07:42.346 --> 00:07:44.600
(audience applause)

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.120
- I'm scared enough right now.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.240
I don't need, I don't need another.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.490
I don't need that.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.160
- Are you serious?

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.110
So wait, Courtney Cox said that

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.170
you'd mess with her on set.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.350
Are you a prankster? Is this true?

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.470
- I'm not really a prankster.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:01.860
She's really very, very easy
to scare as it turns out.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:04.317
So, and I didn't know that.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:08.170
And I, you know, I adore
Courtney is wonderful

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:11.000
and it was so, I had done an
episode of "Friends" years ago.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.380
But we didn't really get to work together

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.830
I've just had so much fun on the show.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:19.980
But yeah, you can scare the
bejesus out of Courtney.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.720
Just at any time, anywhere.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.390
So I use that to great effect.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.120
- Did I hear that you
actually scared her for real,

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.930
and then they ended up using it?

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.950
- Yes, actually, if you watch the trailer

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:33.450
for "Shining Vale,"
it's on the stars thing,

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.090
and if you watch it you'll see,

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.940
the last beat of it is me kind of going up

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.530
and I don't know, I was just
bored and threw it out there.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.030
But she jumps about three
feet high and it was great.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.240
- I'm that person, I hate to be scared.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.350
But I wanna see it.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.003
- [Greg] Yeah. Good, good.

00:08:49.003 --> 00:08:51.960
(door creaking)

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:52.793
(screams)

00:08:52.793 --> 00:08:54.277
- God, why?

00:08:54.277 --> 00:08:55.809
- God, why (laughs).

00:08:55.809 --> 00:08:57.620
(crowd cheering)

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.470
- That is, there's no acting there.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.074
There is no acting, that
is an authentic scare.

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.744
- She literally just yelled "God, why?"

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:06.870
That was amazing.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.030
So you used to have a show just like this,

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:09.863
or it's sorta like this,

00:09:09.863 --> 00:09:12.193
but did you enjoy it or
did it stress you out?

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.000
- I did. I guess I did enjoy it.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.720
I mean, we were on really late at night

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:21.400
and I guess I was, you know, if you,

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.080
as long as you're person you're talking to

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.727
has answers to the questions.

00:09:25.727 --> 00:09:26.790
- Yeah, exactly.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.830
- It's better.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:28.663
- Oh my God.

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:31.180
That's the one thing
whenever I first started,

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.020
I hadn't started yet.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:33.970
And Seth Meyers and Jimmy Fallon,

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.273
everybody kept telling
me, like, I was like,

00:09:35.273 --> 00:09:37.010
well what should I like,
I've never done that.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.370
I don't know why they're giving me a show.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.290
I was like, I don't know what's happening.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.580
And I was like, what
should I look out for?

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.690
And they're like, it's only hard when

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:43.420
you get someone that just is like, yes.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:45.683
And I was like, what?

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:49.878
I feel like I talk enough for
all humans in the room, so.

00:09:49.878 --> 00:09:51.530
(audience applause)

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.100
I wasn't really nervous about that.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.390
But it is funny though.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.160
Are you really in to pop
culture enough to know it?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.940
Because I have to do a lot of homework.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:09:59.950
Did you?

